<p><strong>The Global Desk</strong> is committed to the highest standards of journalistic integrity. Our editorial policy outlines how we gather, verify, and publish news.</p>

<h3>1. Accuracy and Fact-Checking</h3>
<p>Every piece of news published on The Global Desk goes through a verification process. We rely on primary sources, official statements, and trusted news agencies (like Reuters, AP). Unverified rumors are never published as facts.</p>

<h3>2. Independence</h3>
<p>We are an independent platform. We do not accept funding from political parties or governments. Our analysis is unbiased and reflects a global perspective.</p>

<h3>3. Corrections</h3>
<p>If we make a factual error, we will correct it promptly and transparently. We do not delete past articles; instead, we update them with a visible correction note.</p>

<h3>4. AI Usage</h3>
<p>We may use AI tools for drafting and translation, but all final content is reviewed and approved by human editors before publication.</p>